WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.595
Active footprints are created when a person or organization intentionally publishes or submits information.

00:00:06.595 --> 00:00:16.168
Posts, public profiles, comments, photographs, videos, resumes, websites, press releases, issue discussions, and public repositories can all become durable and searchable.

00:00:16.168 --> 00:00:21.061
Intentional sharing does not mean every future use was expected.

00:00:21.061 --> 00:00:29.784
A post written for one audience may be copied, archived, indexed, or viewed years later in a different context.

00:00:29.784 --> 00:00:36.378
Edits and deletion can reduce exposure but may not remove prior copies or references.

00:00:36.378 --> 00:00:40.846
Passive footprints arise through collection, observation, and technical operation.

00:00:40.846 --> 00:00:44.037
Services generate access and security logs.

00:00:44.037 --> 00:00:48.079
Websites and applications may use analytics or tracking.

00:00:48.079 --> 00:00:50.419
Search engines index pages.

00:00:50.419 --> 00:00:52.759
Data brokers compile records.

00:00:52.759 --> 00:00:58.929
Breach notifications may indicate that account data was exposed by a compromised provider.

00:00:58.929 --> 00:01:07.651
People and organizations often underestimate passive exposure because it is distributed across many systems and controlled by third parties.

00:01:07.651 --> 00:01:16.373
Settings may be complex, retention may be unclear, and one service can combine account, device, location, and behavioral data.

00:01:16.373 --> 00:01:19.565
The boundary is not always perfect.

00:01:19.565 --> 00:01:26.159
Uploading a photograph is active, while embedded metadata or subsequent indexing may be passive.

00:01:26.159 --> 00:01:34.882
Creating an account is deliberate, while the service's long-term logging and profiling may not be obvious to the user.

00:01:34.882 --> 00:01:38.498
Managing both types requires awareness and control.

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:48.923
Limit intentional publication to what is necessary, review account and service settings, secure accounts, understand important third-party practices, and monitor for unexpected exposure.

00:01:48.923 --> 00:01:57.219
Do not assume that invisible collection is harmless or that deliberate sharing remains under the original publisher's control.
